From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 07:40:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] netd: do not exit when there is no cgroup v2 root

The 20.0 boot reaches the LineageOS boot animation and stays there. netd is
restarting in a tight loop -- 107 times in ten minutes, each exiting with
status 1:

  netd 1.0 starting
  Netd: Failed to find cgroup v2 root Success
  NetdService: WARNING: returning null INetd instance.

so NetworkManagementService never connects and the framework never finishes
booting.

main.cpp requires the cgroup v2 root and exits when it is absent. This kernel
is 3.10 and cannot mount cgroup2 at all, so cgroups.json declares no v2
hierarchy and the lookup can never succeed here.

Important detail: this exit sits BEFORE libnetd_updatable_init(), so the
BpfHandler degradation added to packages/modules/Connectivity never ran --
netd died two calls earlier. Both changes are required.

cg2_path is left empty and passed through; BpfHandler::init() then fails to
attach and sets mBpfEnabled=false, which is the intended behaviour on a
kernel with no eBPF.
---
 server/main.cpp | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/server/main.cpp b/server/main.cpp
index 0e81d4e5..8067638b 100644
--- a/server/main.cpp
+++ b/server/main.cpp
@@ -126,10 +126,28 @@ int main() {
         gLog.info("setCloseOnExec(%s)", sock);
     }
 
+    // ether/msm8992: do NOT exit when there is no cgroup v2 root.
+    //
+    // cgroup v2 arrived in Linux 4.5; this device runs 3.10, whose kernel cannot mount the
+    // cgroup2 filesystem at all, so cgroups.json declares no v2 hierarchy and this lookup always
+    // fails. Upstream treats that as fatal, which puts netd into a permanent restart loop -- 107
+    // restarts in one 10-minute boot, each ending:
+    //
+    //   netd 1.0 starting
+    //   Netd: Failed to find cgroup v2 root Success
+    //
+    // and system_server never gets an INetd ("WARNING: returning null INetd instance"), so the
+    // device sits on the boot animation forever.
+    //
+    // Note this exit is reached BEFORE libnetd_updatable_init(), so the BpfHandler tolerance added
+    // in the Connectivity patch never gets a chance to run. Both are needed.
+    //
+    // cg2_path is left empty; BpfHandler::init() then fails to attach its programs and degrades to
+    // mBpfEnabled=false, which is exactly the intended path on a kernel with no eBPF either.
     std::string cg2_path;
     if (!CgroupGetControllerPath(CGROUPV2_CONTROLLER_NAME, &cg2_path)) {
-        ALOGE("Failed to find cgroup v2 root %s", strerror(errno));
-        exit(1);
+        ALOGW("No cgroup v2 root (%s) -- continuing without it; BPF-dependent features degrade",
+              strerror(errno));
     }
 
     if (libnetd_updatable_init(cg2_path.c_str())) {
